    <statement><p>Find the curvature of the plane curve
<me>y=t^{2}</me>
at the point <m>t=2</m>.</p>
<p><m>\kappa(2) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.0285336</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>y=f(t)</m> in the plane, we have:
<me>\kappa(t)=\frac{|f''(t)|}{(1+(f'(t))^2)^{3/2}}.</me>
Here <m>f(t)=t^{2}</m>, so <m>f'(t)=2t</m> and <m>f''(t)=2</m>. Hence
<me>\kappa(t)=\frac{2}{\left(1+\left(2t\right)^{2}\right)^{1.5}}.</me>
We evaluate this at <m>t=2</m> to obtain
<me>\kappa(2)=\frac{2 \cdot 2^{0}}{(1+4 \cdot 2^{2})^{3/2}}\approx 0.0285336.</me>


</solution>
